<title>UK: 10 hurt as train hits buffers at London station.</title>
<headline>10 hurt as train hits buffers at London station.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten people were injured on Wednesday when a commuter train with 500 passengers on board hit the buffers at London's Victoria station, officials said.</p>
<p>None of those injured was seriously hurt, said a spokeswoman for the train operator, Connex South Eastern.</p>
<p>The cause of the accident was being investigated.</p>
<p>Fire Brigade official Iain Hunter said he was surprised more people were not hurt, although it was &quot;a slow-moving accident&quot;.</p>
</text>
